h a reason'. ADR: yes — one short record (0007). Gate 1: it sets a boundary (single writer task, close-once state) that the later typed-checker layer, handshake work and core wiring must respect. Gate 2: a reader seeing a channel and a task where a mutex would do will plausibly revert to the mutex; framing.rs's module doc already asserted the false 'no partial-state problem' invariant. Enforced by AC-2/AC-3/AC-7 tests."
